<h1>Geolocation</h1>
<p>
    The map starts hidden. Your location is requested when the page loads, and the
    <strong>location control</strong> puts a marker at it once there is something to show. The marker
    keeps moving if your location changes; the map is only moved the first time, so it doesn't yank
    itself back while you're panning.
</p>
<p>
    The button in the bottom left appears only after a location is found &mdash; deny permission and
    no dead button is left on the map. Clicking it pans back to you. The styling is this page's own;
    the library ships no CSS for controls.
</p>

<style>
    .TestBtn {
        background-color: #fff;
        border: none;
        border-radius: 2px;
        box-shadow: 0 1px 4px -1px rgb(0 0 0 / 30%);
        color: #333;
        cursor: pointer;
        font-family: inherit;
        font-size: 14px;
        margin: 10px;
        padding: 8px 12px;
    }
</style>
<div style="margin: 10px 0">
    <button id="toggleMap" type="button" aria-controls="locateMap" aria-expanded="false">Show map</button>
</div>
<p id="locateStatus" aria-live="polite" style="margin: 10px 0">Requesting your location...</p>
<div id="locateMap" class="mapContainer" hidden></div>

<script src="{{ '/js/geolocation.js'|url|safe}}"></script>
